 "brief_summary": "The purpose of this clinical research study is to learn whether Saxagliptin added to thiazolidinedione (TZD) therapy is more effective than TZD alone as a treatment for Type 2 diabetic subjects who are not sufficiently controlled with TZD alone",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Type 2 diabetics currently receiving a stable dose of TZD monotherapy (pioglitazone 30mg or 45mg, or rosiglitazone 4mg or 8mg) for at least 12 weeks prior to screening.\n* Hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) \\> = 7.0% and \\< = 10.5%\n* Body mass index \\< = 45kg/m2\n* Fasting C-peptide \\> = 1 ng/mL\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Symptomatic poorly controlled diabetes\n* Recent cardiac or cerebrovascular event\n* Serum creatinine \\> = 2.0 mg/dL",
  "sex": "ALL",
  "minimum_age": "18 Years",
  "maximum_age": "77 Years",
  "healthy_volunteers": false,
  "std_ages": [
   "ADULT",
   "OLDER_ADULT"
  ]
 },
